    "title": "How to live stream Yankees vs Giants: MLB, TV channel",
    "text": "The New York Yankees and San Francisco Giants continue their 2026 MLB opening series with Game 2 on Friday at Oracle Park, as New York looks to build early momentum while San Francisco aims to bounce back. MORE: MLB preseason power rankings Advertisement Mar 25, 2026; San Francisco, California, USA; San Francisco Giants second baseman Luis Arraez (1) reacts in front of New York Yankees infielder Jazz Chisholm Jr. (13) after turning a double play in the seventh inning at Oracle Park. Mandatory Credit: Cary Edmondson-Imagn Images How to Watch Yankees vs Giants Date: Friday, February 27, 2026 Time: 4:30 p.m. ET TV Channel: YES, MLB.TV – Giants Live Stream: Fubo (try for free) The Yankees took control of the series in dominant fashion on Opening Night, cruising to a 7-0 win behind a strong all-around performance. Pitcher Max Fried delivered over six scoreless innings, while the offense exploded for a five-run second inning to put the game out of reach early. Advertisement Despite a quiet night from Aaron Judge, New York’s depth was on full display, with contributions throughout the lineup, including timely hitting and aggressive baserunning. Now, the Yankees will look to carry that momentum into Game 2 as they continue their road trip to open the season. Advertisement San Francisco, meanwhile, will try to regroup after a tough opener. The Giants struggled to generate offense in Game 1 and will need a much stronger showing at the plate to even the series. Playing at home in front of their fans, expect a more competitive effort as they aim to avoid falling into an early 0-2 hole. Game 2 is expected to feature a strong pitching matchup, with both teams turning to fresh arms as they settle into the opening weekend of the season. Early-season matchups often come down to execution and bullpen depth, areas where the Yankees showed an edge in the opener. Fans looking to follow the New York Yankees all season can stream games live on Fubo, which carries the YES Network for local broadcasts. For out-of-market coverage, Fubo also offers MLB.TV as an add-on, giving fans access to games from across the league throughout the 2026 season. Regional restrictions may apply. If you purchase a product or register for an account through one of the links on our site, we may receive compensation. — Enjoy free coverage of the top news & trending stories on The Big Lead — MARCH MADNESS: 2026 Sweet 16 TV schedule, game times & dates for NCAA Tournament MLB: Who has the highest Opening Day payroll in MLB? Not the Dodgers NFL: Raiders’ Ashton Jeanty weighs in on Fernando Mendoza-Ty Simpson debate SPORTS MEDIA: 2026 MLB Opening Day TV schedule, full list of games ENTERTAINMENT: 2026 Sports Emmy Awards nominees, full list announced VIRAL: Best & most outrageous MLB ballpark foods for 2026 season",
